## 8. Phases (each ends in a verifiable artifact)

- **P0 — transport.** Dashboard adapter (REST + `/api/ws`) behind the existing `src/api` interface;
  token in `expo-secure-store`; loopback instance + Serve `:10444` documented as setup; `adb reverse`
  in the device-test recipe. Extend `mock/` with the dashboard routes **and** a fake WS dispatch.
  `verify:` rail renders from `/api/profiles` + `/sidebar`; a scripted RPC returns an asset data URL;
  killing `:9118` falls through to the `:9222` candidate and shows *modo reduzido*.
- **P1 — roster parity + F1:** faces with avatars, expand/collapse into sessions, day grouping,
  25/page, dots per §2.1, icon chrome + toolbar (F2).
- **P2 — thread parity + F3:** details expansion (tools/reasoning), live activity over WS, session
  actions via long-press, model lock.
- **P3** search/scope filters with the honest client-side boundary.
- **P4** groups + colours + manual sort (phone-local, D1a).
- **P5** multi-select bulk actions.
- **P6** Apropos (scoped).
- **P7** connections manager (§5) + state card + export log (§9).
- **P8** layout export/import (S2).
- **P9** iOS parity via EAS.
- **P10 (separate goal)** gateway layout blob (S1).

Every phase: git commit, `npm test` green (the existing suite must stay green), `tsc --noEmit` clean.
Android first, then iOS.

---

## 9. Export log — one file, log + your description

- Capped ring buffer (≈500) of structured events: UTC timestamp, level, category
  (`net|auth|api|ws|ui|error`), message; per call: method, path, status, duration, chosen connection,
  attempt #.
- Header: app version + versionCode, build id, device + OS, active connection + candidate list with
  priorities, dashboard host (host only), Tailscale state, last 3 failures.
- **A description box on the export screen** — what you type lands at the top of the file, so one file
  *is* "log + what went wrong".
- Share, don't upload: write `.txt` to the app cache dir → OS share sheet (`expo-sharing`) plus
  copy-to-clipboard. Reachable from Settings **and** the failure banner.
- **Redaction is mandatory and unit-tested:** strip auth headers, api keys, access/refresh tokens,
  `token`/`ticket` values → `[REDACTED]`; never log bodies carrying credentials. A test must assert a
  known secret cannot appear in an exported log — this rule rots silently otherwise.
- Local only. No telemetry, no auto-send.

